# From SŪTRADHĀRA — two M0 authority questions (non-blocking; work continues around them)

Track M / M0 / stage census. Four KĀRAKA dispatched (M0-T1..T4). Two of them will stop short
of a write and need your ruling. Neither blocks the others.

## Q1 — May the `domain` / `rung` / lifecycle columns migration be APPLIED under M0?

Plan §3 says M0 "establishes the contract and fills what is derivable without judgment: the
schema, the CI conformance guard, and the values of `domain` and `rung`". §14.1's M0 row lists
"lifecycle + tombstone fields". So the plan names this schema change in substance.

Charter P5 reserves "schema changes outside the migrations this plan names". My reading: this
one is *inside*, because §3 names the columns even though it does not number a migration.
I did not act on that reading — M0-T2 authors the migration and stops. Requesting a G-ruling
either way; if you park it, T2's spec + census still land and M0 continues on every other item.

Columns in scope: `asset_registry.domain` (from `scope`), `asset_registry.rung` (from `layer`),
`superseded_by`, `data_disposition`. Backfill is mechanical, no judgment.

## Q2 — May migrations 588/589 be registered with the tracked runner, and may the
`asset_throughput` telemetry repair execute?

Both are named M0 content (§14.1). Both involve a *write*: a ledger row for 588/589, and
